{
  "$comment": "Curated routing priors of the Autark project: OUR OWN judgement (public evidence + user experience, state 2026-11-06). NOT Artificial Analysis data. strengths: category -> prior in [-1, 1]. smarts: how capable the model is overall, 0..100, curated from public rankings (LMArena, Artificial Analysis) and our own use – a newer, cheaper model that is as smart ranks above an older, pricier one (Fable 5.1 and GPT-6 Astra sit below Opus 5.5 and GPT-6.1 Sol). relCost: relative marginal price 0..1 – derived from the list prices when both are given ((3 x input + output) / 4 per 1M, $20 = 1.0), else set by hand; subscriptions are discounted by the router while quota remains. First matching entry wins; 'match' is a provider model id or a glob with '*'.",
  "$prices": "Optional per model: priceInputPerM / priceOutputPerM = API list price in USD per 1M input/output tokens; priceCachedInputPerM = the list price per 1M cached input tokens (cache reads), for the cached part of the input the engine reports. Used to book pay-per-use turns whose provider reported no cost (runtime/models/pricing.ts) and shown to the agents (models.list, the models line of 'My environment'). Only verified list prices; leave them out when unsure (a keyless daily OpenRouter price list fills missing ones, runtime/models/price-feed.ts; an unpriced turn is booked with amount 0 and flagged, never guessed).",
